From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cuttlely vendor <vendor@cuttlely.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cuttlely: security pins for Python and JS dependencies

What: raises PyJWT to 2.15.1, httpx2/httpcore2 to 2.13.1, urllib3 to 2.8.0, and adds floors for tornado 6.5.9, oauthlib 4.0.0 and multidict 6.9.1 in pyproject.toml (relocked uv.lock with the pinned uv 0.12.3); raises js-yaml to 4.3.2 in package.json and vitest to 4.1.11 in tests-js/package.json. Why: published security advisories against the previously locked versions (including a critical PyJWT key-confusion issue). Drop this patch once upstream ships these versions.
---
 package.json          |   4 +-
 pyproject.toml        |  34 +--
 tests-js/package.json |   2 +-
 uv.lock               | 558 ++++++++++++++++++------------------------
 4 files changed, 264 insertions(+), 334 deletions(-)

diff --git a/package.json b/package.json
index 2170d11554b26484be7dfd583b665db65782980c..12b8a0ee06e9974bdf3d11a34a24f826f31ec8ce 100644
